<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>French Quarter by Motorbike: Motorbike Parking Guide in Hanoi</h1>
<p>The French Quarter is the calm, formal grid south and southeast of Hoan Kiem Lake, and its parking is exactly what its facades suggest, tidier than the Old Quarter&rsquo;s but still decided at the curb, block by block, hour by hour. The boulevards run wide and shaded, the buildings hold hotels, offices and institutions, and many frontages have their own watched arrangements, which makes the quarter look easy from the saddle and keeps the honest rider asking one small question everywhere the day stops, where does the machine live while I am inside. This guide reads the quarter&rsquo;s parking habits without inventing a single guaranteed spot, because parking in Hanoi is a local fact, not a page&rsquo;s promise, and the reader who leaves with the right questions will park better than the reader who leaves with a list.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the river, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, and the desk&rsquo;s current pointers are part of the plan. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/hoan-kiem-parking-guide/">Hoan Kiem parking guide</a> for the district-wide picture, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/old-quarter-parking-guide/">Old Quarter parking guide</a> for the dense grid at the quarter&rsquo;s shoulder.</p>
